---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import TopNav from '../components/TopNav.astro';

const testAuditAsOf = '2026-04-27';
---

<Base
  title="About — Sebastian Rogala"
  description="Independent product engineer with 12 years of software background, fully AI-directed since early 2026."
>
  <TopNav current="about" />

  <main class="frame">
    <header class="page-header">
      <div class="eyebrow">About</div>
      <h1>Sebastian Rogala</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Independent AI-native product engineer. 12 years of software background. After a
        personal/family pause through end of 2025, fully AI-directed since early 2026. Based in
        Rzeszów, Poland.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="content">
      <h2>How I work now</h2>
      <p>
        I am not looking for a classic senior developer role centred on manual code production. My
        leverage is designing AI-directed delivery systems: turning product intent into structured
        specs, decomposing work for agents, building verification loops, and validating shipped
        outcomes. My core principle: <strong>AI failures are spec gaps, not agent shortcomings.</strong>
        I improve delivery by encoding failure modes structurally — through tests, review agents,
        audit tools, hooks, durable state, and source-cited knowledge.
      </p>

      <h2>Current work</h2>
      <ul class="work-list">
        <li>
          <strong>Education SaaS</strong> — multi-tenant platform, launch customer in production.
          Course management and lead-operations across education tenants; ready for expansion onto
          additional customers. Stack: PHP 8.4 / Symfony 7.4 LTS / Doctrine 3 / PostgreSQL 16 / Redis 7 backend;
          Twig + Stimulus + Turbo + Tailwind front-end; Vitest + PHPUnit + Playwright on tests.
          Hexagonal modular monolith with full CQRS at the UseCase layer, async events via Symfony
          Messenger, 7 business modules. Audit suite green — see screenshot below.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>ProfitOfExile</strong> — public-source Path of Exile lab-farming tool. Built solo
          across Go / SvelteKit / Tauri (Rust) / TimescaleDB — backend, web, desktop overlay. Web
          continuously deployed; desktop overlay shipped from cold start to usable release in ~2
          weeks (v0.1.0 on 2026-03-31 → v0.6.x on 2026-04-13). A single Go backend feeds both the
          web (zero-install SvelteKit) and the Rust/Tauri desktop with OCR and in-game overlays —
          one source of truth, two delivery surfaces. Adopted by the broader community after creator
          coverage.
          <a href="https://profitofexile.top" target="_blank" rel="noopener">profitofexile.top</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Pipeforge</strong> — personal Claude Code orchestration plugin and PostgreSQL MCP
          backend. Pipeline orchestration with templated commands, agent dispatch, skill-based
          prompts, and an MCP-backed tool layer over a PostgreSQL state store — plus a curated
          knowledge base of decisions about Pipeforge itself. Walkthrough at
          <a href="/pipeforge">/pipeforge</a>.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <figure class="audit-figure">
        <a
          href="/screenshots/07-test-audit-all-suites-clean.png"
          class="lightbox-link"
          aria-label="Open full-size screenshot"
        >
          <img
            src="/screenshots/07-test-audit-all-suites-clean.png"
            alt="Test audit on the production Education SaaS: 4,190 PHP tests + 157 E2E, all clean, runtime 7m 13s"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </a>
        <figcaption>
          Test audit on the production Education SaaS (as of {testAuditAsOf}): 4,190 PHP tests + 157 E2E green,
          259 structured learnings logged in 7m 13s. Suites: PHPStan clean · Unit 2674/2674
          (8539 assertions) · Integration 459/459 · Functional 699/699 · Smoke 201/201 · E2E 157/157.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <h2>How quality gets enforced</h2>
      <p>
        The Education SaaS runs four independent custom enforcement layers in CI — every PR has
        to pass all four before it can merge.
      </p>
      <ul class="work-list">
        <li>
          <strong>PHPStan 2 at level 8</strong> — plus 13 project-specific custom rules:
          entity-ID safety, tenant query safety (blocks direct <code>EntityManager</code> /
          <code>Connection</code> access outside repositories), and ADR-shape rules for the
          Action / UseCase / QueryAdapter / Port catalog. The CQRS seam is enforced at this
          layer.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>PHPMD</strong> — hexagonal-tuned ruleset for code smells; complements PHPStan
          on style and maintainability fronts that static analysis doesn't cover.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Deptrac</strong> — enforces 3 hexagonal layers
          (Domain → Application → Infrastructure) across 7 business modules. Vendor imports
          gated by layer; exceptions baselined and documented.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Custom Twig/Tailwind lint script</strong> — 6 project rules expressing UI
          conventions that off-the-shelf linters can't: component-only
          <code>&lt;twig:Button&gt;</code> (no raw <code>&lt;button&gt;</code> in pages),
          semantic-token-only Tailwind (no literal grays), required
          <code>data-component</code> attributes, no manual <code>dark:</code> variants in
          components, ADR-tied destructive-action wrapping, and target-naming in confirmation
          modals. Managed baseline for staged migration with stale-entry detection.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Each layer runs independently; the baseline pattern lets new code raise the bar without
        requiring full migration of legacy code first.
      </p>

      <h2>Public proof &amp; community</h2>
      <ul class="work-list">
        <li>
          <strong>Anthropic Claude Code tracker</strong> — public reproducible investigation isolating
          a compact-vs-clear instruction-override asymmetry in SessionStart hook behavior:
          <a
            href="https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/6354#issuecomment-3849990217"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener">github.com/anthropics/claude-code/issues/6354</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Open-source contributions</strong> — <code>poe-vendor-string</code> PR adding
          prefix/suffix indicators and first tests to the repo; <code>superpowers</code> PR proposing
          smart question batching with empirical <code>AskUserQuestion</code> reduction.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Speaking</strong> — rg-dev Meetup, 27.05.2026 (scheduled), AI-native workflow / migration
          audit talk; Xebia Internal Conference, Nov 2023, <em>GitHub Actions &amp; Continuous Delivery
          on Shared Hosting</em>.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Availability</h2>
      <p>
        Available for AI-native engineering roles, advisory engagements, and team workshops on
        context engineering and AI-directed delivery. The workflow is usually the unfamiliar part —
        happy to walk through it.
      </p>

      <h2>Reach</h2>
      <ul class="reach">
        <li><a href="mailto:sebrogala@gmail.com">sebrogala@gmail.com</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://linkedin.com/in/seb-rogala" target="_blank" rel="noopener">linkedin.com/in/seb-rogala</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/SebRogala" target="_blank" rel="noopener">github.com/SebRogala</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <footer class="page-footer">
      <a href="/">← back home</a>
      <span class="sep">·</span>
      <a href="/pipeforge">Pipeforge walkthrough →</a>
      <span class="sep">·</span>
      <a href="/kb">Knowledge base →</a>
    </footer>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .frame {
    max-width: 1140px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 48px 32px;
  }
  /* Content blocks span the full frame width (matching Home). If specific
     long-form paragraphs need narrower line lengths for readability, cap
     them individually — not at the section level. */

  /* Topnav lives in src/components/TopNav.astro. */
  /* `.sep` is also used in the page footer below — keep as page-level rule. */
  .sep {
    color: var(--rule-2);
  }

  .page-header {
    margin-bottom: 36px;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 11.5px;
    color: var(--muted);
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }
  h1 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 44px;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--fg);
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .lede {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 19px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--fg);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .content {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding-top: 32px;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 15.5px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  .content h2 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: 22px;
    color: var(--fg);
    margin: 32px 0 14px;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .content h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .content p {
    margin-bottom: 14px;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  .content strong {
    color: var(--fg);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .content em {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-style: italic;
  }
  .content code {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--fg-nav);
    background: var(--bg-raise);
    padding: 1px 5px;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }
  .content a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
    text-decoration-color: rgba(125, 179, 108, 0.4);
  }

  .work-list {
    padding-left: 22px;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  .work-list li {
    margin-bottom: 14px;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .audit-figure {
    margin: 12px 0 24px;
  }
  .audit-figure a {
    display: block;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule-2);
    border-radius: 4px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--bg-raise);
    transition: border-color 160ms ease;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .audit-figure a:hover {
    border-color: var(--accent);
  }
  .audit-figure img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }
  .audit-figure figcaption {
    margin-top: 10px;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 13.5px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--fg-nav);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .reach {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 13.5px;
    list-style: none;
    padding-left: 0;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  .reach li {
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }

  .page-footer {
    margin-top: 48px;
    padding-top: 22px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 13px;
    display: flex;
    gap: 12px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .page-footer a {
    color: var(--accent);
    transition: color 160ms ease;
  }
  .page-footer a:hover {
    color: var(--fg);
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .frame {
      padding: 36px 22px;
    }

    h1 {
      font-size: 32px;
    }
    .lede {
      font-size: 16px;
    }
    .content h2 {
      font-size: 19px;
    }
    .content {
      font-size: 14.5px;
    }
  }
</style>
